        "data": {
          "text": "Rank Collapse on real text · TinyShakespeare pretraining (final reproducible setting).\nPaper protocol: intermediate Pythia/OLMo checkpoints, real pretraining corpora, and RankMe/alphaReQ on last-token hidden states evaluated on FineWeb. This Template instead trains a small causal Transformer from scratch on real TinyShakespeare text so the entire pipeline remains editable and runnable in CR. It uses a corpus-derived top-252 word vocabulary plus PAD/BOS/EOS/UNK, 32-token contexts, 4000 windows, d=4, 4 layers, 4 heads, AdamW and next-token CE. RankMe and alphaReQ use every token position as a sample from the explicit final_hidden endpoint. The 20k default is the evidence horizon at which expansion and compression are both fully visible; the smoke test shortens only an in-memory copy.\n\nFinal setting: d_model=4, num_layers=4, num_heads=4, ff_dim=64, context=32, 4000 windows, batch=32, AdamW(lr=5e-3, beta1=.9, beta2=.99, wd=1e-3), 20k updates logged every 100 steps. Weight decay is the sensitive knob: at wd=1e-2 the decay term dominates the narrow d=4 representation and flattens the spectrum before the transient expansion can form, so the collapse never separates from noise; wd<=1e-3 with lr=5e-3 makes the warmup - expansion - compression trajectory unambiguous within 20k steps. Extending to 100k shows a partial rebound after the trough. The Template defaults to cpu for portability; use mps/cuda in the Trainer node if available.",
          "instanceTitle": "Real-text audit - claim boundary",
          "__collapsed": true
        }
      },
